Original commit body from f1beb986925dfb00c4c12a736bac01d1d9a56098:

Three defects the module docstring had been stating as known gaps:

- ``f[x_] := ...``: the left-hand side is a ``call`` node in the grammar,
  so every definition emitted a ``calls`` edge from the file to the
  function it defines. A call on the left-hand side of the nearest
  enclosing ``:=`` / ``=`` (the head, a pattern inside it ``f[g[x_]]``, a
  Part target) now emits nothing.
- Every call edge started at the file node. It now starts at the
  ``function`` symbol of the nearest definition whose body contains it,
  by the definition node's position (``symbols_at``); a variable
  assignment on the way up is walked past; a top-level call keeps the
  file. Dedup is per (source, callee) instead of per (file, callee).
- ``.m`` files that ``classify_dot_m_file`` labels Wolfram were never
  analyzed: ``find_wolfram_files`` existed with no caller. It is now the
  analyzer's ``_find_source_files``; MATLAB and Objective-C ``.m`` files
  stay with their own analyzers, which apply the same classifier.

Red on dev: ``f[x_] := x + 1`` yields ``calls file -> f``; a Wolfram
``.m`` yields no symbols. Six tests pin the new behaviour, including a
resolved call to a project definition, which the self-call from the
definition head had been the only thing covering.

